// APW-5 — Event ordering (A must precede B) — CORRECT variant.
//
// Intent: a `Write` is only well-formed if a `Read` of the same resource has
// occurred first (read-before-write). The `when temporal` clause is a
// `formerly within` whose body is a *conjunction* of two event references —
// the "A && B in the window" shape (distinct from taint-egress, whose body is
// a single event reference).
//
// The correct / buggy distinction is the event kind of the events (mirroring
// the other shapes):
//   * `request`  (CORRECT): the ordering is enforced on the *requested* events
//     -> B is admitted only after A has been requested.
//   * `response` (BUGGY):   the ordering is enforced only on *settled* events
//     -> B can be admitted before A has settled (an out-of-order write).
//
// Schema: Drupe namespace.
// See: rot/shapes.py (build_event_ordering_ir -- the hand-written oracle).
@id("event_ordering_correct")
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Write",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h (
        Drupe::Action::"Read"::request{ input.key: context.input.key }
        && Drupe::Action::"Write"::request{ input.key: context.input.key }
    )
};